Regional Market Insights
•	North America: North America leads the public transport insurance market due to its highly developed infrastructure and stringent regulatory frameworks that prioritize passenger safety and liability coverage. Mature public transportation systems, including extensive bus networks, rail services, and emerging autonomous shuttles, drive consistent demand for comprehensive insurance solutions.
•	Europe: Europe's public transport insurance market thrives on unified EU directives that standardize coverage for cross-border operations, emphasizing environmental compliance and passenger rights. Dense rail and tram networks in countries like Germany and France fuel demand for specialized policies.
•	Asia-Pacific: In Asia-Pacific, the public transport insurance market expands rapidly with urbanization and megacity development in China, India, and Japan. Massive investments in metro expansions and bus rapid transit systems heighten needs for scalable coverage.
•	Latin America (South America): South America's public transport insurance market shows resilience in Brazil and Mexico's bustling bus corridors. Emphasis lies on third-party liability amid rising accident frequencies in informal fleets.
•	Middle East & Africa: The Middle East & Africa public transport insurance market emerges amid oil-driven diversification and African urban booms. Gulf states invest in metro projects, demanding premium coverage for futuristic systems.
